# Build context for service/Dockerfile, whose build context is the
# repository root (`docker build -f service/Dockerfile .`).  Only the
# Go module is copied into the image, so everything else is excluded:
# without this file every build ships the whole tree as its context,
# including local databases, build output and scratch data.
# Go test and fuzz files are never compiled into the service binary;
# excluding them keeps test-only edits from invalidating the image layer
# and keeps test dependencies out of the build context. The patterns
# use wildcards over the Go tree's known package depths, not one entry
# per file, so a newly added test file is excluded by default instead
# of silently re-entering the context until someone notices it here.
# The root .dockerignore carries the same exclusions for the same reason;
# keep the two files' Go-test patterns in sync.
.git
.venv
.venv-fuzz
build
dist
.scratch
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.db
*.sqlite3
data
scale_data
service/*_test.go
service/cmd/*/*_test.go
service/internal/*/*_test.go
